    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 82.38 score against G. Holmes. While Holmes presents a challenge, **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier weapon, buoyed by a favorable matchup and an advantageous spot in the two-hole. **Mickey Moniak** (69.13) and **Seiya Suzuki** (68.78) also project as high-floor, high-ceiling plays; **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing as the wind blowing out at his venue provides a crucial boost to his raw power projection against the right-handed Webb. **Josh Naylor** (72.72) rounds out our top-tier starters, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Wesneski makes him a must-start in this Roto format.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero**, who sat right on the fringe of the starting rotation. While he possesses the requisite speed profile to help us in our scarcest category, his negative platoon adjustment against Fisher dropped him behind the more stable output projected for **Travis Bazzana** and **Cole Young**. Elsewhere, we remain hampered by the health of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, who remain on the IL, alongside **Brice Turang**, who is currently held out of the starting lineup. We continue to monitor the utility slot where **Austin Riley** (60.98) draws a favorable start against Rodriguez, though his position at the bottom of the order slightly mutes his potential for run production.\n\nA final note of caution: while **Max Muncy** (57.50) and **Isaac Paredes** (55.07) are cleared to start, their scores reflect marginal-to-strong value, and their output will be sensitive to their performance against Gore and Hancock, respectively. We are effectively punting on additional speed upside from the bench today, relying instead on the established reliability of our active OF corps. We remain in a holding pattern regarding prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**, alongside veterans **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Zach McKinstry**, who are not in today's active rotation but remain ready for upcoming high-value spot starts.",
